meta {
  name: 11-Register as APPLICANT
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/auth/register
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "temi.adebayo.yaba+{{run_tag}}@gmail.com",
    "password": "Yaba-First-Move-2026!",
    "fullName": "Temi Adebayo",
    "displayName": "Temi A.",
    "phone": "+2348101234567",
    "role": "APPLICANT",
    "publicRole": true
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: in [201, 202]
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 202 || res.status === 201) {
    bru.setVar("temi_email", "temi.adebayo.yaba+" + bru.getEnvVar("run_tag") + "@gmail.com");
    bru.setVar("temi_password", "Yaba-First-Move-2026!");
  }
}

docs {
  Day 2. I came back. I want to save a couple of these places so I
  don't have to scroll-and-find them again. The app says I need an
  account first.

  Picking a real-looking gmail because the spec says strict email
  validation. Phone is a real Nigerian MTN range. Password has 24
  chars with a symbol — should clear the "common password
  blocklist" the persona doc mentions.

  Side note: the spec says this returns 202 with NO body, even on
  success. So I won't get my JWT here — I have to go and log in
  separately. That's a friction surprise vs every other consumer
  app I've used (Cowrywise, Carbon, Kuda) where signup auto-logs me
  in. Will note this in my review.
}
